    "faqs": [
      {
        "q": "What age can a child ride an e-bike?",
        "a": "There is no single age, but children who ride a pedal bike confidently and can use both brakes are ready to try low assistance with supervision. Many families start from about 8 to 10 years old."
      },
      {
        "q": "Do kids need a licence for an e-bike?",
        "a": "Generally no, because a 250 W pedal-assist e-bike that meets the standard is treated as a bicycle. Rules on age and where you may ride vary by state, so check your state authority first."
      },
      {
        "q": "What size e-bike for a 10 year old?",
        "a": "Most 10 year olds fit a 20 to 24 inch frame, but check the rider height range and stand-over height on each product page and test the fit with the child on the bike."
      },
      {
        "q": "Are e-bikes safe for kids?",
        "a": "They can be, when the bike fits, the assistance is low and the child is supervised and wears a helmet. A heavier bike needs more care in braking and handling than a normal bike."
      },
      {
        "q": "What gear should my child wear?",
        "a": "A certified helmet that meets AS/NZS 2063, closed shoes and bright clothing. Gloves and lights add safety, and teens who ride off-road should consider knee and elbow protection as well."
      }
    ],
